 "answer": "Singapore’s latest official readings are **elevated to high for PM2.5, with unhealthy to very unhealthy 24-hour PSI**. At **5:00 a.m. Singapore time on October 16**, 1-hour PM2.5 ranged from **101 µg/m³ in the North** to **161 µg/m³ in Central**; Central had a 24-hour PSI of **219**, in the *very unhealthy* range. ([api-open.data.gov.sg](https://api-open.data.gov.sg/v2/real-time/api/pm25))\n\nReadings vary by region. The NEA classifies 1-hour PM2.5 of **151–250 µg/m³ as “High”**; its PSI scale classifies **201–300 as “Very unhealthy.”** ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/))",
